NVIDIA says its competitive position has already been harmed by export controls, and that its competitive position and future results will be further harmed over the long term if [S3][S4]:
- the restrictions remain in place or are expanded in geographic, customer, or product scope;
- customers purchase product from competitors;
- customers develop their own internal solution;
- NVIDIA is unable to provide contractual warranty or other extended service obligations;
- the USG does not grant licenses in a timely manner, or denies licenses to significant customers;
- NVIDIA incurs significant transition costs.

The filing adds that the licensing process may not be resolved before significant business opportunities evaporate. Even if licenses are granted, they may be temporary, impose burdensome conditions on installation, maintenance and use, or include financial or economic requirements that NVIDIA or its customers cannot or choose not to fulfill [S3][S4].

